.\" openi2pd: i2pd tui.1.
.\"
.\" Configures project configuration and integration.
.\"

.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt I2PD-TUI 1
.Os openi2pd
.Sh NAME
.Nm i2pd-tui
.Nd local ncursesw console for openi2pd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ar path
.Op Fl -datadir Ar directory
.Op Fl -conf Ar file
.Op Fl -service
.Op Fl -help
.Op Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a separate-process ncursesw client for a running
.Xr i2pd 1
router.
It displays router status, peers, tunnels, network database, logs, and native
BitTorrent state.
It does not open router data files, network sockets, download files, or a
JSON-RPC connection.
.Pp
The client communicates only over the local UNIX-domain socket published by
the daemon using the bounded
.Dv I2PDTUI/1
protocol.
The daemon accepts only a peer with its effective UID.
Router views are read-only; torrent start, stop, reannounce, add, and remove
operations require explicit confirmation where they change state.
.Pp
The console never requires a bitmap logo, external font, or truecolor
terminal.
It adapts to monochrome, 8-, 16-, and 256-color terminals.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -socket Ar path
Connect to an explicit UNIX-domain socket.
.It Fl -datadir Ar directory
Resolve the default socket below
.Ar directory .
.It Fl -conf Ar file
Read the
.Ql [tui]
socket setting from this
.Xr i2pd 1
configuration file.
.It Fl -service
Use the system service data directory.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print the client version and exit.
.El
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql q
Quit.
.It Ql Tab , Ql 1 Ns ... Ns Ql 7
Switch views.
.It Ql r
Refresh the current view.
.It Ql ?
Show the help view.
.It Ql /
Filter the torrent list.
.It Ql a , Ql A
Add a magnet link or a local torrent file.
.It Ql p
Start or pause the selected torrent.
.It Ql R
Reannounce the selected torrent.
.It Ql d , Ql D
Remove the selected torrent, optionally with its local data.
.It Ql x , Ql z
Stop all torrents or remove all torrents with confirmation.
.It Ql s
Change torrent sorting.
.It Ql [ , ]
Switch the selected torrent service tunnel.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa i2pd-tui.sock
Default daemon socket, relative to the data directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SECURITY
The client trusts the daemon only after the kernel reports the same effective
UID for the socket peer.
Do not make the socket directory world-writable or copy the socket path into an
untrusted environment.
.Pp
Terminal output is escaped before display so untrusted peer, torrent, and log
text cannot inject terminal control sequences.
Torrent operations remain inside I2P; the console has no clearnet path.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr i2pd 1 ,
.Xr i2pdctl 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
.An openi2pd
